<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's M. Confianca profit up 20 pct.</title>
<headline>Portugal's M. Confianca profit up 20 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending Dec 31</p>
<p>(In billions of escudos unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit     4.22     (Up 20 percent)</p>
<p>    Parent company	3.00     vs     1.7</p>
<p>Note - Insurer Mundial Confianca is the Champalimaud holding company which includes stakes in Banco Pinto &amp; Sotto Mayor, Banco Totta &amp; Acores, Credito Predial Portugues and Banco Chemical  </p>
<p>    Parent premiums    83.00     vs    66.00</p>
<p>    Life premiums	32.80     vs    20.80</p>
<p>    Non-life	     50.20     vs    45.20</p>
<p>    Cons assets	 273.00     vs   235.30</p>
<p>Mundial Confianca's share of the overall insurance market was 8.9 percent -- 7.4 percent in the life sector, and 10.2 percent in the non-life, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
